---
/**
 * The one door out of the prayer-times surface and into the site's actual
 * subject matter.
 *
 * /bonetider/ is by far the largest thing islam.se publishes — the hub, the
 * method page and 2 118 locality pages — and it carries the highest-intent
 * traffic on the site: someone searching "bönetider malmö" is looking for a
 * prayer time, which means they are already interested in the prayer. Until now
 * every exit from those pages led to more prayer times (nearby localities, the
 * method page, the full index) and nothing in the editorial corpus linked in
 * either. A reader could use the site for years and never learn it explains
 * anything.
 *
 * Deliberately three links and no prose. This sits on a utility page whose job
 * is a table of times; an invitation is welcome, a pitch is not.
 *
 * Slugs are real and load-bearing — there is no `vad-ar-bonen` page. The prayer
 * answer is `sa-ber-man-steg-for-steg` ("Hur ber man i islam? Bönen steg för
 * steg"). If one of these is ever renamed, the redirect map in astro.config.ts
 * is the place that keeps this honest.
 */
---

<section class="om-bonen" aria-labelledby="om-bonen-head">
	<h2 id="om-bonen-head">Om bönen</h2>
	<ul class="om-bonen-links">
		<li><a href="/svar/sa-ber-man-steg-for-steg/">Så ber man steg för steg</a></li>
		<li><a href="/svar/islams-fem-pelare/">Islams fem pelare</a></li>
		<li><a href="/vad-ar-islam/">Vad är islam?</a></li>
	</ul>
</section>

<style>
	/* Self-contained on purpose. This renders on three different pages, and Astro
	   scopes a page's <style> to that page's own markup — the host's
	   `.bt-stad-section` / `.bt-stad-section h2` rules do not reach in here. So the
	   section margin and the --step-1 heading are restated rather than inherited,
	   matching what the surrounding sections on /bonetider/<ort>/ look like. */
	.om-bonen {
		margin-top: var(--space-phi);
	}

	.om-bonen h2 {
		font-size: var(--step-1);
	}

	/* The same quiet hairline rows the FAKTA hub uses for its functional lists
	   (.pillar-links) — NOT the pill row the nearby-localities list uses directly
	   above this one. Pills there mean "another place"; these are not places, and
	   giving them the same shape would read as more of the same. */
	.om-bonen-links {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: var(--step--1);
		margin: var(--space-half) 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
		max-width: var(--content-width);
	}

	.om-bonen-links li + li {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
	}

	.om-bonen-links a {
		display: block;
		color: var(--color-accent);
		text-decoration: none;
		/* 0.7rem block padding clears the 24px target floor (WCAG 2.5.8). */
		padding-block: 0.7rem;

		&:hover {
			text-decoration: underline;
			text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
		}

		&:focus-visible {
			border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
		}
	}
</style>
